  <plot>A night-shift keeper tends lantern #4 on a rain-soaked pier while unfinished letters stack beside a brass kerosene lamp. Fog swallows the radio call sign. Four moths hold a census on the glass. The harbor is fictional. The documents stay local. No cloud accounts are opened. The chrome keeps your place; the weather keeps the rest.</plot>
  <outline>A keeper, a lamp, a wet notebook, and a chair that is only a reflection.</outline>
  <tagline>The document is the interface.</tagline>
